1
00:00:05,133 --> 00:00:11,800
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:32,633
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:35,300
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:39,700 --> 00:00:40,833
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:44,133
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:44,133 --> 00:00:45,333
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,333 --> 00:00:46,433
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:46,700 --> 00:00:48,067
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,333 --> 00:00:51,500
- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]

10
00:00:52,433 --> 00:00:53,500
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:54,267 --> 00:00:55,333
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,600 --> 00:00:57,633
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:58,500 --> 00:00:59,833
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:02,400
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,367 --> 00:01:06,333
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:08,533 --> 00:01:09,700
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:11,567
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:11,567 --> 00:01:13,233
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:13,233 --> 00:01:15,433
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:21,433
<i> I had Django summoned.</i>

21
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:22,900
<i>I'll tell Lucas
to check on them.</i>

22
00:01:22,900 --> 00:01:24,300
<i>That's worth more
than your entire existence.</i>

23
00:01:24,300 --> 00:01:25,633
<i> Wait, let me finish this--</i>

24
00:01:25,633 --> 00:01:27,700
<i>They are not enemies.
They have unfinished business.</i>

25
00:01:27,700 --> 00:01:29,300
<i>I heard things got intense
back there.</i>

26
00:01:29,300 --> 00:01:33,633
<i>The case has become
too personal for my agents.</i>

27
00:01:33,633 --> 00:01:35,367
<i>We caught these outsiders
snooping around.</i>

28
00:01:35,367 --> 00:01:37,333
<i>They look innocent.
We have to help them.</i>

29
00:01:37,333 --> 00:01:38,733
<i> Pops sent us here.</i>

30
00:01:38,733 --> 00:01:42,200
Tomorrow we'll send the details
of your mission to your tablet.

31
00:01:42,233 --> 00:01:44,167
<i>I'll do everything
to succeed in my mission.</i>

32
00:01:44,167 --> 00:01:45,667
<i>I am just going to look
for a job.</i>

33
00:01:45,667 --> 00:01:46,767
<i> It's a legal job, right?</i>

34
00:01:46,767 --> 00:01:48,200
<i> When we have a family,</i>

35
00:01:48,200 --> 00:01:49,700
<i>I want to give you all
a good life.</i>

36
00:01:50,267 --> 00:01:51,667
[ELTON] You know, Rudy,

37
00:01:51,667 --> 00:01:53,600
I don't think those guys
are capable of anything.

38
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:55,400
Just look at them.
They look like beggars,

39
00:01:55,400 --> 00:01:56,833
and their clothes
are all torn up.

40
00:01:56,833 --> 00:01:58,233
They look starving.

41
00:01:58,233 --> 00:01:59,900
Why'd you beat them up?

42
00:01:59,900 --> 00:02:01,700
That's what Gabo told us to do.

43
00:02:02,667 --> 00:02:04,733
Alright, we're going inside.

44
00:02:04,733 --> 00:02:06,133
- Later.
- Alright.

45
00:02:11,100 --> 00:02:13,233
Oh, what's...

46
00:02:13,233 --> 00:02:15,833
What's this? Why didn't they
finish their food?

47
00:02:15,867 --> 00:02:19,567
Oh! What a waste...

48
00:02:19,567 --> 00:02:21,267
Oh, no. Eventually,

49
00:02:21,267 --> 00:02:23,833
we'll have to start counting
our sardines around here.

50
00:02:24,433 --> 00:02:26,600
Oh, Gabo...

51
00:02:27,600 --> 00:02:34,233
Gabo, why'd you let people in
this early?

52
00:02:34,633 --> 00:02:38,400
You trust people way too easily.

53
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:42,267
What if they're thieves
or dangerous people?

54
00:02:42,267 --> 00:02:44,600
And you just let them
into the house.

55
00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:45,633
[DANTE] Yeah, Gabo.

56
00:02:45,633 --> 00:02:47,500
We shouldn't trust people
so easily.

57
00:02:48,267 --> 00:02:49,367
But, Uncle...

58
00:02:50,433 --> 00:02:51,867
I felt sorry for them

59
00:02:52,567 --> 00:02:54,733
because my friends
beat them up.

60
00:02:54,733 --> 00:02:56,233
And they were starving.

61
00:02:56,667 --> 00:02:59,767
So I let them into the house
so I could feed them.

62
00:03:00,400 --> 00:03:02,533
You know, Gabo's right.

63
00:03:03,467 --> 00:03:06,367
When someone is hungry,
we should feed them.

64
00:03:06,967 --> 00:03:09,567
When someone asks for help,
we should help them too.

65
00:03:10,467 --> 00:03:13,267
Let's not assume the worst
about others.

66
00:03:13,333 --> 00:03:16,533
We should be thinking about
how we can help them.

67
00:03:17,433 --> 00:03:19,933
Now, if they do something bad,

68
00:03:20,933 --> 00:03:22,467
that's Gabo's problem.

69
00:03:23,367 --> 00:03:24,633
If they're capable
of doing that.

70
00:03:26,200 --> 00:03:29,800
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

71
00:03:31,833 --> 00:03:33,900
Didn't we already search
Calle Soriano?

72
00:03:34,700 --> 00:03:36,267
Crisologo!

73
00:03:36,933 --> 00:03:38,300
Buong Diwa!

74
00:03:38,600 --> 00:03:40,633
There's only one place left

75
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:42,967
in our two-kilometer
search area.

76
00:03:42,967 --> 00:03:44,700
Ginintuang Lupa!

77
00:03:44,700 --> 00:03:48,767
You think Sam went
to Ginintuang Lupa?

78
00:03:48,767 --> 00:03:50,667
We all know

79
00:03:50,667 --> 00:03:52,600
everyone there hates
the Jacinto family...

80
00:03:52,600 --> 00:03:54,467
Well, if Sam's desperate,

81
00:03:54,500 --> 00:03:56,533
it's not impossible
that she'd hide there.

82
00:03:56,533 --> 00:03:58,233
If she hid in Ginintuang Lupa,

83
00:03:58,233 --> 00:03:59,700
she might be dead
by the time we find her.

84
00:03:59,700 --> 00:04:01,400
Don't say that!

85
00:04:01,400 --> 00:04:02,733
Sam's still alive!

86
00:04:02,733 --> 00:04:05,033
If our team leader
weren't taking it so easy,

87
00:04:05,033 --> 00:04:06,467
I'd believe you!

88
00:04:06,467 --> 00:04:08,500
- Are you questioning me?
- [DELGADO] Enough!

89
00:04:09,867 --> 00:04:11,967
Will you two stop fighting?

90
00:04:12,033 --> 00:04:18,867
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

91
00:04:24,367 --> 00:04:27,300
Sir, this has gotten
too personal for the team.

92
00:04:27,300 --> 00:04:29,733
We're not thinking clearly
anymore.

93
00:04:29,767 --> 00:04:31,867
Sir, we're sorry.

94
00:04:32,367 --> 00:04:35,867
Castor, saying sorry
won't fix this mess.

95
00:04:38,500 --> 00:04:40,067
Sir, may I suggest something?

96
00:04:40,067 --> 00:04:42,067
Let's hand the search
for Jacinto

97
00:04:42,067 --> 00:04:43,933
over to another team.

98
00:04:43,933 --> 00:04:46,367
But they're the best in NCIA.

99
00:04:46,733 --> 00:04:47,867
In my opinion?

100
00:04:49,700 --> 00:04:50,867
It doesn't look like it.

101
00:04:50,867 --> 00:04:54,933
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

102
00:04:54,933 --> 00:04:56,300
Well, Pia...

103
00:04:56,733 --> 00:04:58,600
Put together a new team.

104
00:04:58,600 --> 00:05:01,733
We can't stop looking for Sam!

105
00:05:01,767 --> 00:05:02,967
- Sir?
- Sir!

106
00:05:02,967 --> 00:05:04,033
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

107
00:05:06,600 --> 00:05:09,433
Maybe you need
to take a breath

108
00:05:10,967 --> 00:05:12,733
and get some rest first.

109
00:05:12,733 --> 00:05:17,333
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

110
00:05:18,867 --> 00:05:21,433
Guys, let's talk to Sir Delgado.

111
00:05:21,433 --> 00:05:23,800
- We can still change his mind.
- Karen.

112
00:05:23,800 --> 00:05:25,433
Ma'am Pia is probably right.

113
00:05:25,433 --> 00:05:28,300
I don't think we're fit
or capable of doing the job.

114
00:05:28,300 --> 00:05:30,067
If you're frustrated because
we haven't gotten any results

115
00:05:30,067 --> 00:05:33,100
from everything we've done,
just think about one thing.

116
00:05:33,100 --> 00:05:35,400
We're looking for our friend!

117
00:05:35,767 --> 00:05:38,667
Sam needs us to stick together
more than ever right now.

118
00:05:38,667 --> 00:05:40,467
So fix your issues.

119
00:05:40,467 --> 00:05:42,433
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

120
00:05:42,900 --> 00:05:44,400
[TEKLA] Hey, Gabo.

121
00:05:44,400 --> 00:05:45,733
What's your plan?

122
00:05:49,967 --> 00:05:53,833
You'd better go back
to your posts.

123
00:05:53,833 --> 00:05:56,933
I think you just misunderstood
those people.

124
00:05:57,433 --> 00:05:58,667
They're actually nice.

125
00:05:58,667 --> 00:06:00,133
They're just hungry.

126
00:06:00,133 --> 00:06:01,500
That's what I thought!

127
00:06:01,500 --> 00:06:02,667
I knew it!

128
00:06:02,667 --> 00:06:04,633
You guys were too hot-headed.

129
00:06:04,633 --> 00:06:06,133
You immediately suspected them.

130
00:06:06,133 --> 00:06:08,633
You even messed
with those scavengers.

131
00:06:08,667 --> 00:06:09,967
And we're the hot-headed ones?

132
00:06:09,967 --> 00:06:11,700
Weren't you the first one
to get worked up?

133
00:06:11,700 --> 00:06:13,167
- He's right.
- Me?

134
00:06:13,167 --> 00:06:15,100
You didn't even get to know them
You attacked them right away.

135
00:06:15,100 --> 00:06:17,800
Hey, we were just testing you.

136
00:06:17,800 --> 00:06:19,967
That means you weren't focused.

137
00:06:19,967 --> 00:06:21,133
That's why you ended up
fighting!

138
00:06:21,133 --> 00:06:22,533
Besides, it was
the right thing to do

139
00:06:22,533 --> 00:06:24,500
- so we wouldn't get outsmarted.
- Right.

140
00:06:24,500 --> 00:06:26,633
You'd better get back
to your posts.

141
00:06:26,633 --> 00:06:28,433
Our enemies might slip away.

142
00:06:28,433 --> 00:06:29,967
- Go on.
- Can't we eat first?

143
00:06:29,967 --> 00:06:31,667
- No, let's get back.
- Come on!

144
00:06:31,667 --> 00:06:33,867
- Come on!
- You're not family. Let's go.

145
00:06:33,867 --> 00:06:35,033
Come on!

146
00:06:35,033 --> 00:06:37,967
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

147
00:06:40,800 --> 00:06:42,100
Uh, Pa?

148
00:06:42,867 --> 00:06:45,700
Tomorrow, I'm going out.

149
00:06:46,500 --> 00:06:48,000
I'm just going to look
for a job.

150
00:06:50,133 --> 00:06:51,200
Really?

151
00:06:51,200 --> 00:06:54,533
You're looking for a new job?

152
00:06:54,533 --> 00:06:55,700
That's good.

153
00:06:55,700 --> 00:06:59,400
- I hope you find a good one.
- That's right.

154
00:06:59,400 --> 00:07:02,633
That way, Betchay won't always
hold it over our heads.

155
00:07:02,633 --> 00:07:04,833
But, Gabo...

156
00:07:05,500 --> 00:07:07,800
What about Gloria?

157
00:07:08,867 --> 00:07:10,533
Uh...

158
00:07:10,533 --> 00:07:12,367
Auntie, if it's okay,

159
00:07:12,900 --> 00:07:15,200
could you stay with Gloria
tomorrow

160
00:07:15,233 --> 00:07:16,867
while I look for a job?

161
00:07:16,867 --> 00:07:18,433
Oh, of course.

162
00:07:18,433 --> 00:07:21,767
But Gloria, is it okay with you
that you're here

163
00:07:21,767 --> 00:07:23,733
without Gabo around?

164
00:07:23,733 --> 00:07:25,533
Of course. [CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

165
00:07:25,533 --> 00:07:28,067
Oh, that's good to hear!

166
00:07:28,067 --> 00:07:32,100
I'll teach you to cook
a lot of home-cooked meals.

167
00:07:32,100 --> 00:07:33,567
That'd be nice.

168
00:07:33,567 --> 00:07:34,700
[ALL CHUCKLE SOFTLY]

169
00:07:36,500 --> 00:07:37,467
Sir?

170
00:07:38,767 --> 00:07:40,533
Can we talk to you?

171
00:07:42,033 --> 00:07:49,033
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

172
00:07:56,867 --> 00:07:59,467
Uh, we know

173
00:07:59,467 --> 00:08:02,000
that you're considering
Ma'am Pia's advice.

174
00:08:03,100 --> 00:08:06,600
I hope you'll still let us
work on this case.

175
00:08:07,467 --> 00:08:09,100
And we promise that...

176
00:08:10,267 --> 00:08:12,233
we'll all get our acts together.

177
00:08:12,233 --> 00:08:14,533
We want to do this for Sam.

178
00:08:14,533 --> 00:08:17,667
Sir, I know
we had our differences.

179
00:08:18,933 --> 00:08:20,600
But we can set it aside
for this.

180
00:08:22,633 --> 00:08:24,233
My decision to distance you

181
00:08:24,233 --> 00:08:26,700
from a case
you're getting too involved in

182
00:08:28,967 --> 00:08:30,267
is for Sam's sake.

183
00:08:31,167 --> 00:08:32,833
Sir, with all due respect,

184
00:08:32,833 --> 00:08:35,733
but Team Alpha
is the best team in NCIA.

185
00:08:35,733 --> 00:08:37,900
I hope you reconsider.

186
00:08:37,900 --> 00:08:39,233
We're doing this for Ma'am Sam.

187
00:08:40,267 --> 00:08:41,667
Sir.

188
00:08:41,667 --> 00:08:45,967
I know you still believe
in Team Alpha to find Sam.

189
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:55,600
Get your act together.

190
00:08:59,933 --> 00:09:01,533
This is for Sam.

191
00:09:01,533 --> 00:09:03,567
Ginintuang Lupa is vast.

192
00:09:04,533 --> 00:09:06,133
Scour the whole area!

193
00:09:07,333 --> 00:09:08,667
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

194
00:09:08,667 --> 00:09:12,533
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

195
00:09:12,533 --> 00:09:13,767
[MUSIC FADES]

196
00:09:21,700 --> 00:09:22,867
[DRAWER OPENS]

197
00:09:22,867 --> 00:09:29,833
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

198
00:09:33,300 --> 00:09:38,733
[DIGITAL TRILLING]

199
00:09:38,733 --> 00:09:41,833
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

200
00:09:44,067 --> 00:09:49,833
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

201
00:09:50,333 --> 00:09:51,333
[MAX] Attorney.

202
00:09:52,067 --> 00:09:53,633
Here are the documents.

203
00:09:54,333 --> 00:09:55,433
- [ENVELOPE RUSTLES]
- Thank you.

204
00:09:56,067 --> 00:09:58,033
Do you need me to come with you?

205
00:09:58,733 --> 00:10:01,000
No. I can handle this myself.

206
00:10:01,533 --> 00:10:03,200
- Alright, ma'am.
- Okay.

207
00:10:04,733 --> 00:10:11,733
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

208
00:10:16,533 --> 00:10:18,200
You're going to have
to be careful here.

209
00:10:19,033 --> 00:10:21,733
The residents of Ginintuang Lupa
are mad at the Jacintos.

210
00:10:21,733 --> 00:10:24,167
If someone
becomes suspicious of us,

211
00:10:24,167 --> 00:10:26,500
Sam will be in danger.

212
00:10:28,400 --> 00:10:30,333
[SEQIOA]
<i> Okay, guys. Let's just focus.</i>

213
00:10:31,067 --> 00:10:32,400
Keep our eyes open.

214
00:10:32,400 --> 00:10:34,667
Don't worry, Bullet.
I can concentrate,

215
00:10:34,700 --> 00:10:36,600
even when it's chaotic here.

216
00:10:37,400 --> 00:10:38,500
I just don't know
about the others.

217
00:10:39,133 --> 00:10:41,000
You've been pissing me off
since earlier.

218
00:10:41,467 --> 00:10:43,433
[CASTOR]
Hey, you're at it again.

219
00:10:44,400 --> 00:10:45,767
Stop it.

220
00:10:45,767 --> 00:10:50,100
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

221
00:10:50,100 --> 00:10:51,167
[PIA] Sir?

222
00:10:53,600 --> 00:10:56,367
I've already created a team
to replace Team Alpha.

223
00:10:56,367 --> 00:10:58,700
Sebrano will be their leader.

224
00:10:59,300 --> 00:11:00,633
No need.

225
00:11:00,633 --> 00:11:05,100
Tell them to go back
to handling their previous case.

226
00:11:07,133 --> 00:11:10,433
What about our search
for Jacinto?

227
00:11:10,467 --> 00:11:14,333
I gave back the mission
to Team Alpha.

228
00:11:14,333 --> 00:11:16,133
They are the ones most eager...

229
00:11:17,133 --> 00:11:19,433
...to find Sam.

230
00:11:22,167 --> 00:11:23,600
[DELGADO]
They will do everything...

231
00:11:25,433 --> 00:11:27,600
...to find their friend.

232
00:11:32,333 --> 00:11:39,300
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

233
00:11:46,800 --> 00:11:48,800
We've been searching
for hours.

234
00:11:48,800 --> 00:11:51,533
- And we've found nothing.
- What's wrong with you, Reyes?

235
00:11:51,533 --> 00:11:53,667
You know we can't stop
until we've searched

236
00:11:53,667 --> 00:11:55,867
every corner of Ginintuang Lupa.

237
00:11:55,867 --> 00:11:57,833
We made a promise
to Sir Delgado, remember?

238
00:11:57,833 --> 00:11:59,533
Based on our analysis,

239
00:11:59,533 --> 00:12:02,467
this is the only place left
that Sam could've possibly been.

240
00:12:03,600 --> 00:12:05,667
[SEBASTIAN] Then let's search
this entire place.

241
00:12:05,667 --> 00:12:07,167
Come on, let's head there.

242
00:12:08,267 --> 00:12:09,433
[CASTOR] Come on, let's go.

243
00:12:09,433 --> 00:12:16,400
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

244
00:12:20,500 --> 00:12:21,733
[MUSIC TURNS UNEASY]

245
00:12:21,733 --> 00:12:23,500
[DRAWER CREAKS, THUDS]

246
00:12:24,500 --> 00:12:30,733
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

247
00:12:30,733 --> 00:12:31,700
[SHEATH CLOSES]

248
00:12:34,900 --> 00:12:36,200
- [SAM] Oh.
- Love.

249
00:12:37,200 --> 00:12:38,267
What are you doing?

250
00:12:38,733 --> 00:12:41,567
Uh, nothing!
[CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

251
00:12:41,567 --> 00:12:44,733
I'm just checking the stuff I
need to bring to work tomorrow.

252
00:12:44,733 --> 00:12:46,333
- [KNIFE THUDS]
- Tomorrow?

253
00:12:46,333 --> 00:12:48,233
Aren't you supposed
to look for a job?

254
00:12:48,267 --> 00:12:50,600
- Why will you bring those?
- Oh, you know.

255
00:12:50,600 --> 00:12:53,367
I might get into trouble.

256
00:12:53,367 --> 00:12:55,700
I mean, there are a lot
of bad guys these days.

257
00:12:55,700 --> 00:13:00,167
They might start harassing me,
but, see, they won't beat me.

258
00:13:00,167 --> 00:13:03,167
[OBJECTS CLATTERING]

259
00:13:03,167 --> 00:13:04,167
[SHEATH CLOSES]

260
00:13:04,167 --> 00:13:05,900
- [OBJECTS CLATTER]
- Uh, love?

261
00:13:05,900 --> 00:13:10,267
Speaking of tomorrow,
I have to leave early.

262
00:13:10,267 --> 00:13:13,167
You might still be sleeping
by the time I leave,

263
00:13:13,167 --> 00:13:14,433
but I won't wake you up anymore.

264
00:13:14,433 --> 00:13:15,400
[SAM EXHALES]

265
00:13:15,900 --> 00:13:17,267
Are you excited about tomorrow?

266
00:13:17,267 --> 00:13:18,400
Absolutely!

267
00:13:18,400 --> 00:13:20,433
Of course,
I'll finally have work,

268
00:13:20,433 --> 00:13:23,700
and I want you
to be proud of me.

269
00:13:23,733 --> 00:13:27,467
I mean, of course,
now that I'm married,

270
00:13:27,467 --> 00:13:31,200
you can boast about me
for having a job.

271
00:13:31,200 --> 00:13:32,600
And I'll finally be able
to help Papa!

272
00:13:32,600 --> 00:13:33,567
[SAM CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

273
00:13:34,367 --> 00:13:35,700
[GABO CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

274
00:13:35,700 --> 00:13:36,600
Love?

275
00:13:37,433 --> 00:13:38,867
When I have a job,

276
00:13:38,867 --> 00:13:43,200
I want to come home
with you always freshly bathed,

277
00:13:43,200 --> 00:13:44,600
so that-- Don't worry!

278
00:13:44,600 --> 00:13:46,900
I'll always bring home something
for you.

279
00:13:46,900 --> 00:13:48,200
Mmm.

280
00:13:48,733 --> 00:13:52,267
Uh, Gabo, tomorrow,
while you're out,

281
00:13:52,267 --> 00:13:55,467
just so I don't get bored,
can I clean around the house?

282
00:13:55,500 --> 00:13:57,733
Oh, no! I'll do it!
Just wait for me to get home.

283
00:13:57,733 --> 00:14:00,433
I'll clean the whole house,
so you won't get tired.

284
00:14:00,433 --> 00:14:01,667
No, it's okay.

285
00:14:01,667 --> 00:14:03,333
But since you did offer,

286
00:14:03,333 --> 00:14:05,500
do you want
to start cleaning now?

287
00:14:05,500 --> 00:14:06,967
- Now?!
- Mm-hmm.

288
00:14:06,967 --> 00:14:08,500
It's up to you.

289
00:14:08,500 --> 00:14:09,867
Can we start with your room?

290
00:14:10,833 --> 00:14:12,667
Why? The room's clean.

291
00:14:12,667 --> 00:14:16,333
Well, it looks like
a delivery helper's room.

292
00:14:16,333 --> 00:14:19,300
But, love, this is art!

293
00:14:19,300 --> 00:14:20,733
I mean, you can see
how I designed

294
00:14:20,733 --> 00:14:22,267
and painted this room.

295
00:14:22,267 --> 00:14:23,900
I exerted so much effort.
This is art!

296
00:14:24,600 --> 00:14:26,533
- Mmm...
- Why?

297
00:14:27,300 --> 00:14:29,467
Do you want us to paint it
a different color?

298
00:14:29,500 --> 00:14:32,033
Pink, yellow, or green?

299
00:14:32,033 --> 00:14:35,300
Oh, no. Let's just do this
for now.

300
00:14:35,300 --> 00:14:39,367
Let's change the sheets
and the curtains.

301
00:14:39,367 --> 00:14:40,800
Come on, let's change it.

302
00:14:40,800 --> 00:14:43,800
But I just changed the sheets.
That's only been three months.

303
00:14:44,467 --> 00:14:45,700
[SAM CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

304
00:14:45,700 --> 00:14:46,900
Three months?

305
00:14:47,767 --> 00:14:49,700
Let's change it.
It's been a while.

306
00:14:49,700 --> 00:14:50,867
Come on.

307
00:14:50,867 --> 00:14:53,333
A-Alright. Whatever--
Whatever you want.

308
00:14:53,333 --> 00:14:56,333
Whatever you say,
whatever you want,

309
00:14:56,333 --> 00:14:57,767
I'll do it, love.

310
00:14:57,767 --> 00:14:59,333
[GABO CHUCKLES]

311
00:14:59,333 --> 00:15:01,867
But, later, it's nice to sleep
when the sheets are fresh.

312
00:15:01,900 --> 00:15:03,500
And when you're freshly bathed.

313
00:15:03,500 --> 00:15:04,633
Huh? Huh?

314
00:15:05,500 --> 00:15:07,833
Go on.
Look for new sheets, okay?

315
00:15:08,800 --> 00:15:11,333
- Curtain and bed sheet.
- Mm-hmm.

316
00:15:11,333 --> 00:15:12,367
Right away.

317
00:15:14,400 --> 00:15:15,467
[SAM SIGHS]

318
00:15:15,467 --> 00:15:16,467
[TOWEL THUDS]

319
00:15:16,467 --> 00:15:22,933
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

320
00:15:25,800 --> 00:15:28,833
[ARTURO] Sir, we now have the
floor plan of the safe house.

321
00:15:30,800 --> 00:15:35,533
[OBJECTS CLANK, THUD]

322
00:15:37,700 --> 00:15:41,700
Because Django wasn't successful
in retrieving the gold,

323
00:15:41,700 --> 00:15:45,400
the NLEA was able to bring those
to their safe house.

324
00:15:45,400 --> 00:15:49,000
They store all high-value
evidence in that safe house.

325
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:51,467
This is the floor plan
of that safe house.

326
00:15:52,333 --> 00:15:53,833
Want us to raid it, boss?

327
00:15:55,333 --> 00:15:58,367
That place is heavily guarded.

328
00:15:58,367 --> 00:16:01,500
A lot of people are guarding it,
not just those from NLEA.

329
00:16:01,500 --> 00:16:05,000
Besides, their security system
is strict.

330
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:07,600
You can't just walk in there.

331
00:16:07,600 --> 00:16:08,633
Ma.

332
00:16:09,367 --> 00:16:10,667
I'll take care of it.

333
00:16:11,933 --> 00:16:13,567
I already have a plan for that.

334
00:16:13,567 --> 00:16:20,500
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

335
00:16:21,267 --> 00:16:23,000
[OBJECT THUDS]

336
00:16:23,767 --> 00:16:25,400
We'll enter here.

337
00:16:25,400 --> 00:16:27,300
- Norris.
- Yes.

338
00:16:27,300 --> 00:16:29,367
Stallone. You'll enter first.

339
00:16:29,367 --> 00:16:32,033
Our guns are of higher caliber
than theirs.

340
00:16:32,033 --> 00:16:33,633
If there's
a security guard here,

341
00:16:33,633 --> 00:16:35,000
blow up the area
with a grenade.

342
00:16:35,900 --> 00:16:38,033
I'm sure the others will escape
through here.

343
00:16:38,033 --> 00:16:40,700
But, Lee,
we'll go through here...

344
00:16:41,733 --> 00:16:43,567
...so we can retrieve the gold.

345
00:16:43,567 --> 00:16:45,567
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

346
00:16:45,567 --> 00:16:46,900
[MARIANO] If that's the case...

347
00:16:46,900 --> 00:16:47,867
- Arturo.
- Sir.

348
00:16:48,567 --> 00:16:50,067
Give weapons
to Django and his men.

349
00:16:50,067 --> 00:16:51,233
Yes, sir.

350
00:16:55,567 --> 00:16:56,633
[CRATE LID THUDS]

351
00:16:56,633 --> 00:17:03,667
[GUNS CLANKING]

352
00:17:03,667 --> 00:17:06,433
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

353
00:17:06,433 --> 00:17:09,567
Boss, these rifles are
of high caliber.

354
00:17:09,567 --> 00:17:10,933
- [DJANGO CHUCKLES]
- [GUN COCKS]

355
00:17:12,500 --> 00:17:13,633
[GUN THUDS]

356
00:17:13,633 --> 00:17:14,567
Wait.

357
00:17:15,433 --> 00:17:16,667
Do you know how to use that?

358
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:19,000
[DJANGO SCOFFS]

359
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:20,767
We don't need these.

360
00:17:20,767 --> 00:17:22,000
What?

361
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:24,633
We are not getting into
a shootout with the NLEA!

362
00:17:26,600 --> 00:17:27,633
Why?

363
00:17:27,633 --> 00:17:29,000
What's your plan?

364
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:34,700
[INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING]

365
00:17:34,700 --> 00:17:37,100
We're going up against
a powerful agency.

366
00:17:37,100 --> 00:17:39,467
That's why we'll come
heavily armed!

367
00:17:39,467 --> 00:17:41,700
And then what'll happen
when we open fire?

368
00:17:41,700 --> 00:17:43,600
What do you think
they'll do?

369
00:17:43,600 --> 00:17:45,600
They'll call in for backup.

370
00:17:45,600 --> 00:17:47,300
They'll outnumber us.

371
00:17:47,300 --> 00:17:52,300
We can't call for
reinforcements like they can.

372
00:17:52,333 --> 00:17:53,900
They also know
their way around the area.

373
00:17:53,900 --> 00:17:56,867
They'll find a way
to corner us in.

374
00:17:56,867 --> 00:17:59,033
We might not make it out alive.

375
00:17:59,033 --> 00:18:02,800
(In English)
So what's your brilliant idea?

376
00:18:02,800 --> 00:18:03,967
[SCOFFS]

377
00:18:07,733 --> 00:18:09,800
(In Filipino)
Come again?

378
00:18:09,800 --> 00:18:11,400
[SCOFFS]

379
00:18:11,400 --> 00:18:12,767
[SIGHS SHARPLY]
Jeez.

380
00:18:13,500 --> 00:18:17,400
(In Filipino)
What's your plan?

381
00:18:17,400 --> 00:18:19,033
Ah...

382
00:18:19,033 --> 00:18:20,467
We'll wait.

383
00:18:20,467 --> 00:18:21,967
Wait for what?

384
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:24,100
For the guards to change shifts.

385
00:18:24,100 --> 00:18:25,600
It's a safe house.

386
00:18:25,600 --> 00:18:30,033
The same guards
aren't stationed there all day.

387
00:18:30,033 --> 00:18:32,733
They take turns
coming in and out.

388
00:18:33,400 --> 00:18:34,833
And when that happens,

389
00:18:34,833 --> 00:18:36,767
that's when we make our move.

390
00:18:36,767 --> 00:18:38,333
That's when we strike.

391
00:18:39,100 --> 00:18:40,667
That's your plan?!

392
00:18:40,667 --> 00:18:42,633
[DJANGO CHUCKLES, CLAPS]

393
00:18:43,667 --> 00:18:45,733
Why go at them head-on

394
00:18:45,733 --> 00:18:47,833
when we can take them
by surprise?

395
00:18:47,833 --> 00:18:50,900
[LAUGHING]

396
00:18:50,900 --> 00:18:52,900
- [GLASS THUDS]
- Bravo!

397
00:18:52,900 --> 00:18:54,433
That's a solid plan!

398
00:18:54,433 --> 00:18:57,667
Weapons
can only take you so far.

399
00:18:58,967 --> 00:19:02,900
We need to think strategically.

400
00:19:08,900 --> 00:19:10,033
[GUN COCKS]

401
00:19:10,033 --> 00:19:14,900
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

402
00:19:14,900 --> 00:19:18,533
You'd be wrong to think
you don't need a weapon.

403
00:19:18,533 --> 00:19:20,633
Because when
the situation calls for it,

404
00:19:20,633 --> 00:19:22,633
your brain can't protect you
from a hail of bullets.

405
00:19:22,633 --> 00:19:26,700
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

406
00:19:26,700 --> 00:19:29,400
You need to be ready
to use both.

407
00:19:31,667 --> 00:19:34,000
That is, if...
you can handle it.

408
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:35,033
Hmm?

409
00:19:36,933 --> 00:19:38,700
Go. Get ready.

410
00:19:40,967 --> 00:19:42,467
[GUN THUDS]

411
00:19:42,467 --> 00:19:46,733
[TENSE MUSIC SWELLS]

412
00:19:48,133 --> 00:19:53,167
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

413
00:19:53,167 --> 00:19:55,633
Here it is,
Your Majesty!

414
00:19:55,633 --> 00:19:59,067
Here is everything
you asked for!

415
00:19:59,067 --> 00:20:00,633
What's your choice?

416
00:20:00,633 --> 00:20:04,433
Pink? Brown? Green? Or blue?

417
00:20:04,467 --> 00:20:06,033
- Take your pick!
- [SAM CHUCKLES]

418
00:20:06,033 --> 00:20:07,600
Lots of choices!

419
00:20:07,600 --> 00:20:08,800
Um...

420
00:20:08,800 --> 00:20:11,100
I think this one's perfect,
love.

421
00:20:11,100 --> 00:20:14,500
Brown is a masculine color.

422
00:20:14,500 --> 00:20:17,100
It'll make our bed
look so manly.

423
00:20:17,100 --> 00:20:18,167
What do you think?

424
00:20:18,167 --> 00:20:20,267
I think we should avoid
dark colors.

425
00:20:20,267 --> 00:20:23,600
Let's go for colors
that'll brighten your room.

426
00:20:23,600 --> 00:20:25,633
- Oh. You don't like brown?
- Let's keep looking.

427
00:20:25,633 --> 00:20:26,933
Rejected!

428
00:20:26,933 --> 00:20:28,267
[CHUCKLES]

429
00:20:28,267 --> 00:20:30,000
What about pink?

430
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:30,967
Look at that.

431
00:20:30,967 --> 00:20:34,033
This is perfect
for the curtains!

432
00:20:34,033 --> 00:20:36,833
It's an awesome color.
What do you think?

433
00:20:36,867 --> 00:20:38,133
[SAM] Um...

434
00:20:38,133 --> 00:20:40,200
Let's keep looking, okay?

435
00:20:40,200 --> 00:20:41,867
You don't like pink?

436
00:20:41,867 --> 00:20:44,967
What about this?
Yellow! Ha!

437
00:20:44,967 --> 00:20:48,133
Look!
It's perfect, isn't it?

438
00:20:48,133 --> 00:20:49,900
I think that'll do.

439
00:20:49,900 --> 00:20:52,000
- Let's try installing it.
- All right.

440
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:54,500
Uh... Gabo?

441
00:20:54,500 --> 00:20:55,700
What about this?

442
00:20:55,700 --> 00:20:57,633
Can we get rid of it?

443
00:20:57,633 --> 00:20:59,233
My punching bag?

444
00:20:59,233 --> 00:21:02,067
Oh, my love...
I don't think so.

445
00:21:02,067 --> 00:21:03,900
I use that all the time.

446
00:21:03,900 --> 00:21:07,033
When I get into a fight
or I'm angry

447
00:21:07,033 --> 00:21:09,000
I throw a few punches
before I go to sleep.

448
00:21:09,033 --> 00:21:10,833
That's how I let my anger out!

449
00:21:10,833 --> 00:21:12,900
But Gabo, this isn't a gym.

450
00:21:12,900 --> 00:21:16,100
Like you said,
this is our bedroom.

451
00:21:16,100 --> 00:21:17,600
[WHIMSICAL MUSIC PLAYING]

452
00:21:17,600 --> 00:21:19,667
But...

453
00:21:19,667 --> 00:21:22,033
What do I do
when I'm pissed off?

454
00:21:22,033 --> 00:21:24,167
How am I going
to blow off steam?

455
00:21:24,167 --> 00:21:29,933
[WHIMSICAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

456
00:21:29,933 --> 00:21:31,567
But, okay.

457
00:21:32,667 --> 00:21:35,667
If that's what you want,
then I'll make it work.

458
00:21:35,667 --> 00:21:37,667
Just help me
when I need a...

459
00:21:37,667 --> 00:21:38,833
release.

460
00:21:38,833 --> 00:21:41,033
You know my temper.

461
00:21:41,033 --> 00:21:44,033
I'll need some help
letting that out some days.

462
00:21:45,700 --> 00:21:47,100
I mean...

463
00:21:47,100 --> 00:21:50,067
Who else is going to help me,
am I right?

464
00:21:50,067 --> 00:21:52,267
- [SAM CHUCKLING]
- Right? [GUSHES]

465
00:21:52,267 --> 00:21:54,967
All right, let's work on
our love nest.

466
00:21:54,967 --> 00:21:57,200
- I like the sound of that.
- Mm-hmm.

467
00:21:57,200 --> 00:22:00,600
I'll take it down. But if I need
to blow off some steam...

468
00:22:00,600 --> 00:22:02,033
- You know what to do.
- [SAM CHUCKLES]

469
00:22:02,033 --> 00:22:04,567
- Hmm? [EXCLAIMS]
- All right, Gabo.

470
00:22:04,567 --> 00:22:05,867
[GUSHING]

471
00:22:05,867 --> 00:22:08,867
Yes! Yes! Yes!

472
00:22:08,867 --> 00:22:11,600
[COMICAL MUSIC PLAYING]

473
00:22:11,600 --> 00:22:12,600
I'm taking it down.
[CHUCKLES]

474
00:22:12,600 --> 00:22:14,133
[SAM]  What a fool.

475
00:22:14,133 --> 00:22:18,367
<i>He caved in so easily
when I used the wife card.</i>

476
00:22:18,400 --> 00:22:22,200
<i>I think I know how
to get some intel from him.</i>

477
00:22:23,233 --> 00:22:24,400
You done?

478
00:22:24,400 --> 00:22:28,267
I use this punching bag
all the time.

479
00:22:28,267 --> 00:22:30,900
- [SAM CHUCKLES NERVOUSLY]
- So once I put it down,

480
00:22:30,900 --> 00:22:33,067
you know
what comes next, okay?

481
00:22:33,067 --> 00:22:34,767
- [CHUCKLING AWKWARDLY]
- [GABO GUSHING]

482
00:22:34,767 --> 00:22:37,167
Here I go.

483
00:22:37,167 --> 00:22:40,667
[SINGING]
<i> This for you!</i>

484
00:22:40,667 --> 00:22:43,800
[GRUNTING LOUDLY]

485
00:22:46,767 --> 00:22:48,733
[GRUNTS]

486
00:22:48,767 --> 00:22:50,267
I have a new workout now!

487
00:22:50,267 --> 00:22:51,933
Mwah! Mwah! Mwah!

488
00:22:51,933 --> 00:22:53,633
Yay!

489
00:22:53,633 --> 00:22:56,100
[WOMAN] Hey, you two!
Hurry up!

490
00:22:56,100 --> 00:22:58,733
- [MAN 1] Wait!
- [MAN 2] Hold on!

491
00:23:04,767 --> 00:23:06,967
[WOMAN] Look! Over there!

492
00:23:06,967 --> 00:23:08,767
- What is it?
- Is that a body?

493
00:23:08,767 --> 00:23:09,967
- What?!
- Over there!

494
00:23:09,967 --> 00:23:12,867
- [WOMAN] I'm not sure, though.
- [MAN 2] Where?

495
00:23:12,867 --> 00:23:14,833
[WOMAN]
But it looks like a body.

496
00:23:14,833 --> 00:23:15,833
Right there!

497
00:23:15,833 --> 00:23:17,700
At the very edge.
Check it out!

498
00:23:17,700 --> 00:23:19,167
What are
you talking about?

499
00:23:19,167 --> 00:23:21,167
- Where?!
- [WOMAN] It looks like a body!

500
00:23:21,167 --> 00:23:22,600
- Look.
- What's going on?

501
00:23:24,867 --> 00:23:26,033
Right there!

502
00:23:26,033 --> 00:23:27,967
- I think it is a body!
- [MAN 1] Where?!

503
00:23:27,967 --> 00:23:29,967
- Go check if it's a body!
- What's happening?

504
00:23:29,967 --> 00:23:31,167
Let's check it out.

505
00:23:31,167 --> 00:23:32,667
- [MAN 1] Where?!
- [MAN 2] We can't find it!

506
00:23:32,667 --> 00:23:35,667
[WOMAN] Keep looking!
I think that's a red jacket!

507
00:23:35,667 --> 00:23:37,200
Straight ahead!

508
00:23:37,200 --> 00:23:38,667
[MAN 2] Where is it?

509
00:23:38,667 --> 00:23:40,133
- [MAN 1] Yeah!
- Straight ahead!

510
00:23:40,133 --> 00:23:41,800
- What's going on, ma'am?
- Where?!

511
00:23:41,800 --> 00:23:43,700
- I think that's a person.
- That?

512
00:23:43,700 --> 00:23:45,333
It's wearing a red jacket.

513
00:23:48,033 --> 00:23:55,000
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

514
00:24:09,433 --> 00:24:16,467
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

515
00:24:25,700 --> 00:24:27,167
That's Sam's jacket.

516
00:24:28,400 --> 00:24:35,333
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

517
00:24:47,700 --> 00:24:48,433
[GABO] There we go!

518
00:24:48,433 --> 00:24:49,733
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

519
00:24:49,733 --> 00:24:51,533
Whoo! Nice!

520
00:24:51,533 --> 00:24:52,533
[SAM CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

521
00:24:52,533 --> 00:24:55,633
Oh, oh, oh!

522
00:24:55,633 --> 00:24:57,800
Look at it, love.

523
00:24:57,800 --> 00:25:00,933
See? It suits well here.
Look around.

524
00:25:00,933 --> 00:25:04,467
Our room looks like
a work of art.

525
00:25:04,500 --> 00:25:07,633
- [SAM CHUCKLES]
- It now has a masculine touch.

526
00:25:07,633 --> 00:25:09,800
This is nice! Hmm!

527
00:25:09,800 --> 00:25:11,367
[EXCLAIMS] Nice!

528
00:25:14,667 --> 00:25:16,433
Woo-hoo!

529
00:25:16,433 --> 00:25:18,567
It's all clean now

530
00:25:18,567 --> 00:25:19,933
and somehow...

531
00:25:19,933 --> 00:25:21,567
[SNIFFS] smells better.

532
00:25:21,567 --> 00:25:23,067
It doesn't smell
like petrichor anymore.

533
00:25:23,067 --> 00:25:24,467
[BOTH CHUCKLE]

534
00:25:25,800 --> 00:25:27,600
Uh, love?

535
00:25:27,600 --> 00:25:29,667
[MUSIC TURNS SOFT]

536
00:25:29,667 --> 00:25:31,400
Thanks a lot.

537
00:25:31,400 --> 00:25:35,267
You've been a huge help
here at home.

538
00:25:36,500 --> 00:25:38,800
To be honest,
since you got here,

539
00:25:39,633 --> 00:25:41,800
a lot has changed.

540
00:25:42,933 --> 00:25:44,033
If it weren't for you,

541
00:25:44,033 --> 00:25:47,933
I wouldn't have thought
of cleaning my room.

542
00:25:47,933 --> 00:25:51,767
And now, you even
put up some decorations.

543
00:25:51,767 --> 00:25:54,500
It feels more
like a bedroom now.

544
00:25:55,633 --> 00:25:57,000
Uh...

545
00:25:57,000 --> 00:26:00,000
I'd also like to thank you
for being kind...

546
00:26:01,600 --> 00:26:03,367
to my whole family,

547
00:26:03,367 --> 00:26:05,067
especially to our neighbors.

548
00:26:07,867 --> 00:26:09,667
You've no idea

549
00:26:09,700 --> 00:26:12,767
how much
we're grateful for that.

550
00:26:13,967 --> 00:26:15,733
[GABO BREATHES DEEPLY]

551
00:26:15,733 --> 00:26:17,833
Thank you for coming
into our lives.

552
00:26:19,867 --> 00:26:21,633
You know, love,

553
00:26:21,633 --> 00:26:24,700
our home didn't
look like this before.

554
00:26:24,700 --> 00:26:26,333
This is where I grew up.

555
00:26:26,333 --> 00:26:31,033
These walls were then
just made of wood.

556
00:26:31,033 --> 00:26:34,467
And that used to be
a dilapidated iron roof.

557
00:26:34,467 --> 00:26:35,967
Same thing with our neighbors.

558
00:26:36,833 --> 00:26:38,667
But as you can see,

559
00:26:38,667 --> 00:26:41,467
we managed to build the house
slowly with concrete this time.

560
00:26:41,467 --> 00:26:43,467
It's getting more sturdy.

561
00:26:44,533 --> 00:26:45,700
And stronger.

562
00:26:46,600 --> 00:26:47,667
I wish...

563
00:26:51,000 --> 00:26:53,067
I wish that
for our future family, too.

564
00:26:54,033 --> 00:26:56,067
We can start small.

565
00:26:57,533 --> 00:26:59,467
What matters is we're together.

566
00:27:01,500 --> 00:27:02,733
We support each other

567
00:27:03,600 --> 00:27:04,733
and have each other's backs.

568
00:27:07,933 --> 00:27:08,967
You know, love,

569
00:27:10,500 --> 00:27:12,467
later on...

570
00:27:14,767 --> 00:27:16,333
if we decide to have kids,

571
00:27:18,933 --> 00:27:21,567
I want to become
someone you'd be proud of.

572
00:27:23,867 --> 00:27:25,833
I want to give you a good life.

573
00:27:31,467 --> 00:27:32,667
To be honest,

574
00:27:35,033 --> 00:27:37,533
I never thought
you'd come into my life.

575
00:27:40,767 --> 00:27:41,867
I hope...

576
00:27:44,800 --> 00:27:46,700
I hope this isn't just a dream.

577
00:27:49,900 --> 00:27:52,133
I'm hoping that whatever it is
I'm feeling right now...

578
00:27:53,900 --> 00:27:55,567
stays forever.

579
00:27:58,733 --> 00:28:00,533
Gloria, I want you to know

580
00:28:01,833 --> 00:28:03,100
that I love you so much.

581
00:28:05,967 --> 00:28:08,033
I am grateful to God for that.

582
00:28:15,500 --> 00:28:16,567
Gloria.

583
00:28:19,967 --> 00:28:21,033
I love you.

584
00:28:26,467 --> 00:28:33,433
["KUNG KAILANGAN MO AKO"
BY GARY VALENCIANO PLAYING]

585
00:28:47,700 --> 00:28:52,433
<i> My agents found Sam's jacket.</i>

586
00:28:52,433 --> 00:28:53,967
<i> I don't think she survived.</i>

587
00:28:53,967 --> 00:28:54,933
<i> Good news.</i>

588
00:28:54,933 --> 00:28:57,667
<i> Team Alpha lost an agent.</i>

589
00:28:57,700 --> 00:28:59,667
The NCIA abandoned my daughter.

590
00:28:59,667 --> 00:29:02,067
<i>You knew how dangerous
the Zafra case was!</i>

591
00:29:02,067 --> 00:29:03,333
<i> And now she's gone!</i>

592
00:29:03,333 --> 00:29:05,400
<i>Don't forget
that I'm the boss here.</i>

593
00:29:05,400 --> 00:29:08,367
<i>The moment you defy me,
I'll get rid of you myself.</i>

594
00:29:08,367 --> 00:29:10,000
<i> I promise.</i>

595
00:29:10,000 --> 00:29:12,500
<i>You're the only woman
I'd love forever.</i>
